		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=30679#p30679"><![CDATA[
To make this stable you will need a direct matrix solver. You can also try to solve a weld joint as a block of 6x6 matrices. This will give you some stiffness as well. <br><br>In a real world example you would not use a weld joint, but use a compound shape with three boxes.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14">Dirk Gregorius</a> — Fri May 10, 2013 4:19 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
